  "question": {
    "text": "A body of mass <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn><mo> </mo><mi>kg</mi></math> begins to move under the action of a time dependent force given by <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mover><mi>F</mi><mo>→</mo></mover><mo>=</mo><mfenced><mrow><mn>6</mn><mi>t</mi><mo> </mo><mover><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">i</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>+</mo><mn>6</mn><msup><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo> </mo><mover><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">j</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></mrow></mfenced><mo> </mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">N</mi></math>. The power developed by the force at the time <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>t</mi></math> is given by:"
